        {
          "id": "ch14_ex10_q2a",
          "number": "2(a)",
          "category": null,
          "questionText": "Given that $0 < \\theta < \\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\cos\\theta = \\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$, find the value of $\\theta$.",
          "questionFigures": [],
          "solution": {
            "formula": "$\\sin\\phi = \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\phi\\right)$.",
            "steps": [
              "Given: $\\cos\\theta = \\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6}$, $\\theta$ acute. Goal: $\\theta$.",
              "$\\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6} = \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} - \\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\cos\\frac{\\pi}{3}$.",
              "So $\\cos\\theta = \\cos\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ with both angles in $\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$, hence $\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$.",
              "Check: $\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{3} = \\frac{1}{2} = \\sin\\frac{\\pi}{6}$."
            ],
            "finalAnswer": "$\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
            "solutionFigures": [],
            "tip": "Cosine is one-to-one on $\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$, so equal cosines mean equal angles there."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "ch14_ex10_q2b",
